IMPORTANT: replace this file with the real license text before publishing.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Do NOT hand-copy the license text from memory or an AI-generated summary —
legal documents need to be exact. Get the real text one of these ways:

1. Easiest: when creating the GitHub repository, GitHub's own UI has an
   "Add a license" step — choose "GNU Affero General Public License v3.0"
   and GitHub writes the exact, correct, complete text into LICENSE for you
   automatically. No copy-pasting needed.

2. Or visit https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt yourself in a browser
   and save it as LICENSE in this folder.

Either way takes under a minute and guarantees the text is correct.
